{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789210737,"nonce":"chAym3zauerPVB6/YA6HGZtFo5E=","title":"./x and ../x registered as two modules; `is` failed across the boundary","message":"Closed 2026-09-12: no longer reproduces at 5792bac (interpreter and tiered). Fixing commit not identified; repro kept below in case it regresses.\n\n\nInside `@hatch:web/web.wren`:\n\n```wren\nimport \"./live\" for Sse, SseStream   // ← \"./live\" is this module's view\n// ...\nstatic coerce(value) {\n  if (value is SseStream) { ... }     // ← matches when caller came in via web.wren\n}\n```\n\nWhen a handler imports `../live` directly and passes an SseStream to\n`Response.coerce`, the `is SseStream` inside `coerce` is **false**\neven though `value is SseStream` at the handler's top-level is **true**.\nSymptom: SSE responses stringify into \"instance of SseStream\" in the\nplain-Response path because the switch-case never fires.\n\n\nThe engine keys its module registry by the import NAME, not the\nresolved path:\n\n- `import \"./live\"` → registry key `\"./live\"`\n- `import \"../live\"` → registry key `\"../live\"`\n\nBoth loads read the same file, parse it, and produce separate\n`ObjClass` objects. `is` is a pointer comparison, so\n`sse1.class != sse2.class` even though the source is identical.\n\n`src/runtime/engine.rs` stores `engine.modules: HashMap\u003cString,\nModuleEntry\u003e` keyed by the requested-name string; `make_module_loader`\nin `src/main.rs` resolves paths for reading but doesn't canonicalise\nthe registry key.\n\n\nRe-export the classes from one canonical module and have all\nconsumers import through that name. @hatch:web now:\n\n- keeps `./live` as the internal source of Sse / SseStream /\n  Channel / Scheduler_\n- re-exports them via `web.wren`'s `import \"./live\"` so examples\n  that `import \"../web\" for ... Sse, SseStream` see the same\n  class pointer coerce uses.\n\nExample chat.wren:\n```wren\nimport \"../web\" for App, Response, Css, Sse   // ← single import path\n```\n\n\nNormalise `name` to a canonical path (e.g. via\n`fs::canonicalize`) BEFORE inserting into `engine.modules` and\nbefore each `engine.modules.get` call.  Gated by the running file's\ndir for relative paths (already threaded through `LoadModuleFn`\nsince the 2026-04-25 importer-dir fix). Scoped names\n(`@hatch:foo`) already use their literal string, which is fine\nsince they're global.","files":null}]}